---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { u } from '../../lib/url';
---
<Base
  title="Disclaimer and terms"
  description="What this site is, what it is not, and the terms under which you use it."
>
  <div class="shell railed flow dsc">
    <span class="rail-mark" aria-hidden="true">§</span>
    <h1>Disclaimer and terms</h1>
    <p class="lead">Short, because a disclaimer nobody reads protects nobody.</p>

    <h2>This is reference material, not training</h2>
    <p>
      Reading this site does not make you trained, qualified, certified, or approved to
      run a chainsaw. It issues no certificate, keeps no record, and awards nothing. If
      you need a credential — for an employer, an agency, or an insurer — it comes from a
      real course with a real evaluation, not from a web page.
    </p>

    <h2>Chainsaw work is dangerous and this site cannot make it safe</h2>
    <p>
      Chainsaws injure and kill experienced people. Storm debris adds stored energy,
      unstable ground and hidden utilities to that. Nothing here removes those risks.
      Every decision to make a cut is yours, made with your own eyes on your own job,
      and you are responsible for it.
    </p>

    <h2>Your manual and your crew boss outrank this site</h2>
    <p>
      Where this site and your saw's manual disagree, the manual wins. Where this site
      and your employer's, agency's or crew's rules disagree, they win. Where a figure
      here is marked
      <a href={u('/about/verify/')}>unverified</a>, treat it as a prompt to look it up,
      not as an answer.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      This site is provided as-is, with no warranty of any kind, express or implied,
      including accuracy, completeness, or fitness for a particular purpose. To the
      fullest extent permitted by law, the authors and contributors accept no liability
      for any loss, injury, or damage arising from the use of, or reliance on, anything
      published here.
    </p>

    <h2>Power lines</h2>
    <p>
      The <a href={u('/modules/12-downed-power-lines/')}>downed power lines</a> module
      states one rule with no exceptions: assume every line is energized, stay 30 feet
      back, and never cut anything touching or able to reach a line. If any other page
      here appears to soften that, the power line module is correct and the other page is
      wrong — tell us and it gets fixed.
    </p>

    <h2>Content and code</h2>
    <p>
      Content is licensed <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY
      4.0</a>: use it, adapt it, translate it, fork it for your island, with attribution.
      Code is MIT. Fonts are used under the SIL Open Font License. Third-party assets are
      listed with their licenses in <code>ASSET_LICENSES.csv</code> in the repository.
    </p>
    <p>
      STIHL and ECHO are trademarks of their respective owners. They are used here
      nominatively, to describe real products people own. No endorsement, sponsorship or
      affiliation is claimed or implied, and no manufacturer logo, brand color, or
      manual artwork appears anywhere on this site.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      No accounts, no cookies, no analytics, no tracking, no ad networks, and nothing is
      sent anywhere when you use the tools — the STIHL decoder, the chain finder, the
      rotation timer and the checklists all run entirely on your own device. Checklist
      ticks and the rotation timer are stored in your browser's local storage and never
      leave it. That is why there is no cookie banner.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If something here is wrong, it matters more than most websites being wrong. Open an
      issue at <a href="https://github.com/mechaloctopus/chainsaw/issues">github.com/mechaloctopus/chainsaw</a>,
      and say which page and what is wrong with it.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .dsc { padding-top: 2rem; }
  .dsc h2 { font-size: var(--text-h3); }
</style>
